---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
---

<BaseLayout title="Unpeeragogy" description="Peeragogy, up close. Theory, experience, and friction side by side.">
  <section class="py-8 sm:py-16 text-center" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">
    <img src="/images/UnPeeragogy-logo-test.webp" alt="Unpeeragogy" class="mx-auto h-24 sm:h-40 w-auto" />
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg sm:text-xl d-text-sec max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 font-medium">
      Peeragogy, up close.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg d-text-dim max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 mt-2">
      Theory, experience, and friction side by side.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-3 sm:gap-4 px-4">
      <a href="/introduction/" class="rounded-lg bg-(--color-accent) px-6 py-3 text-white font-semibold hover:bg-(--color-accent-light) transition-colors">
        Explore the patterns ⿻
      </a>
      <a href="/why/" class="rounded-lg border border-stone-300 d-border px-6 py-3 font-semibold hover:bg-stone-100 d-hover transition-colors">
        Why this project →
      </a>
      <a href="/vault/" class="rounded-lg border border-stone-300 d-border px-6 py-3 font-semibold hover:bg-stone-100 d-hover transition-colors">
        <Icon name="mingcute:safe-box-line" size={20} class="inline-block align-middle mr-1.5" aria-hidden="true" /> Knowledge Base →
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base d-text-dim max-w-lg mx-auto px-4 mt-6 italic">
      This is not a debunking. It's critical love.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-8">Main Sections</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <a href="/introduction/" class="pattern-card">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Introduction</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">The starting point. What the theory promises and what emerges when you look closely.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/motivation/" class="pattern-card">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Motivation</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">An exploration of what happens to motivation when ideal conditions fall away.</p>
      </a>
      <div class="pattern-card">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-accent)"><a href="/patterns/" class="hover:underline">Peeragogy in Practice</a></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">Patterns, coordination, friction. What works, what warps, and why it's worth looking at.</p>
        <span class="text-xs text-(--color-accent) mt-2 inline-block opacity-70">📄 Success cases: <a href="/newcomer-where-it-works/" class="hover:underline">Newcomer</a> · <a href="/cooperation-where-it-works/" class="hover:underline">Cooperation</a></span>
      </div>
      <a href="/convening/" class="pattern-card">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Convening a Group</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">Bringing people together is simple. Keeping the group together is another story. Observations on the limits of consensus.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/organizing/" class="pattern-card">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Organizing a Learning Context</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">Organizing is necessary. When does it become micromanagement? When does structure help, and when does it replace initiative?</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/cooperation/" class="pattern-card">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Cooperation</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">Cooperation is an ideal. In practice, it produces tension, competition, and unspoken conflict. An analysis.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The Audit</h2>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-6">
      In 2026, after months of silence in the human laboratory, I turned the machines on. Six agents, five pipeline stages, 88 nodes of the Peeragogy Handbook — and a systematic, reproducible, evidence-anchored audit report.
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 max-w-3xl">
      <a href="/audit/" class="p-5 border border-amber-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-amber-50 dark:bg-(--red-bg) hover:brightness-95 transition-all">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">📊 Full Audit Report</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">304 evidence items across 52 entities. 50 distinct source URLs. Mean raw tension delta: +0.027. The full pipeline, results, and reproducibility manifest.</p>
        <span class="text-xs text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 mt-2 inline-block">Read the report →</span>
      </a>
      <div class="p-5 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <h3 class="font-semibold">⚙️ What was done</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">A multi-agent pipeline: Interpretation → Evidence Hunter → Grounding Gate → Critical Analysis → Tension Computation. Every step recorded. Every source traced. The model may propose; the evidence must dispose.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What is Unpeeragogy?</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="p-6 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">📖 Left Column — Peeragogy</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">The historical texts of the Peeragogy Handbook. The theory, the patterns, the vision of collaborative learning. Unchanged, respected — made available so readers can compare them with experience.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 border border-amber-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-amber-50 dark:bg-(--red-bg)">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">⚡ Right Column — Unpeeragogy</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm d-text-sec">Observations, doubts, failure modes, counterexamples. Not a refutation of the theory, but a stress test — to see where it holds and where the gap between theory and experience becomes visible.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm">
      <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 d-surface px-3 py-1">CC Zero — Public Domain</span>
      <a href="/perturbator/" class="rounded-full bg-amber-50 dark:bg-(--red-bg) text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 px-3 py-1 hover:brightness-95 transition-all">Perturbator: friction as epistemic function</a>
      <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 d-surface px-3 py-1">Dual-column reading</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Source ≠ Interpretation</h2>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-6">
      A structural principle of the project: always distinguish what the theory actually says
      from what we observe happening — and from our interpretation of that observation.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-sm">
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <span class="font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Source</span>
        <p class="mt-1 d-text-dim">What the original text actually says. The pattern, the quote, the principle.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <span class="font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">Observation</span>
        <p class="mt-1 d-text-dim">What was observed in experience: a behavior, a dynamic, a friction.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <span class="font-semibold">Interpretation</span>
        <p class="mt-1 d-text-dim">How we read that observation. A hypothesis, not a conclusion.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <span class="font-semibold">Failure Mode</span>
        <p class="mt-1 d-text-dim">A way in which a pattern can degrade or fail under certain conditions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What would change my mind?</h2>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-4">
      UnPeeragogy does not exist to collect examples that confirm its critiques.
      The project must be willing to change its position in the face of counterexamples,
      positive experiences, new data, alternative interpretations.
    </p>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-6 text-sm italic">
      Here are the first two cases where the theory holds. The conditions are still being mapped.
      <a href="/vault/" class="text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 hover:underline">Failure modes</a> remain the project's main purpose — but without success cases, it's not research.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm">
      <a href="/newcomer-where-it-works/" class="p-5 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">✅ Newcomer — the Charlotte Pierce case</h3>
        <p class="d-text-dim">A concrete story of successful onboarding: Charlotte arrives on Google Plus, gets welcomed, becomes a contributor, organizer, and moderator. The pattern works when the group's culture precedes the pattern.</p>
        <span class="text-xs text-(--color-accent) mt-2 inline-block">Read →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/cooperation-where-it-works/" class="p-5 border border-amber-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-amber-50 dark:bg-(--red-bg) hover:brightness-95 transition-all">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 mb-2">✅ Cooperation — the domain where it holds</h3>
        <p class="d-text-dim">A structural analysis of the preconditions: modular work, shared vision, accepted asymmetry. Cooperation emerges when the cost of not coordinating is low.</p>
        <span class="text-xs text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 mt-2 inline-block">Read →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm d-text-dim italic max-w-2xl">
      We are testing the patterns, not processing them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border text-center">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The Path</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:gap-8 text-sm sm:text-base">
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface min-w-[160px]">
        <div class="font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">Peeragogy</div>
        <div class="d-text-dim text-xs mt-1">The first framework</div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-2xl d-text-dim">⟶</div>
      <div class="p-4 border border-amber-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-amber-50 dark:bg-(--red-bg) min-w-[160px]">
        <div class="font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">UnPeeragogy</div>
        <div class="d-text-dim text-xs mt-1">The stress test</div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-2xl d-text-dim">⟶</div>
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface min-w-[160px]">
        <div class="font-semibold">Pyragogy</div>
        <div class="d-text-dim text-xs mt-1">New questions</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm d-text-dim max-w-xl mx-auto">
      Every question generates another question. Not a replacement, but a progression.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How to read Unpeeragogy</h2>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-6">
      This is not a manual against Peeragogy. It is a manual that asks Peeragogy:
      <em>Where do you hold? Where do you give? What conditions do you assume are true? What happens when those conditions aren't true?</em>
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
      <div class="p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface">
        <span class="font-semibold">📖 Left column</span>
        <p class="mt-1 d-text-dim">The theory as it is. The patterns, the quotes, the principles of the Peeragogy Handbook — unchanged.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 border border-amber-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-amber-50 dark:bg-(--red-bg)">
        <span class="font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">⚡ Right column</span>
        <p class="mt-1 d-text-dim">Observations from the field. Failure modes, counterexamples, and the Perturbator asking: <em>what if the theory didn't see this?</em></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 p-4 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface text-sm">
      <p class="d-text-sec">
        <strong>If you read Unpeeragogy and conclude "Peeragogy is wrong," we failed.</strong><br>
        If you read Unpeeragogy and understand <em>"Peeragogy is useful in X, less in Y, and doesn't explain Z"</em>, you got the project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Suggested Path</h2>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-6">
      New to Unpeeragogy? Read in the suggested order:
    </p>
    <ol class="max-w-xl mx-auto space-y-3 text-sm">
      <li class="p-3 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="font-bold text-(--color-accent) text-lg shrink-0 w-6">1</span>
        <div>
          <a href="/introduction/" class="font-semibold hover:text-(--color-accent) transition-colors">Introduction</a>
          <p class="d-text-dim">The starting point. The theory and where the friction begins.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="p-3 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="font-bold text-(--color-accent) text-lg shrink-0 w-6">2</span>
        <div>
          <a href="/motivation/" class="font-semibold hover:text-(--color-accent) transition-colors">Motivation</a>
          <p class="d-text-dim">The first confrontation between expectations and operational reality.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="p-3 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="font-bold text-(--color-accent) text-lg shrink-0 w-6">3</span>
        <div>
          <a href="/patterns/" class="font-semibold hover:text-(--color-accent) transition-colors">Peeragogy in Practice</a>
          <p class="d-text-dim">Patterns, coordination, friction. The heart of the project.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="p-3 border border-stone-200 d-border rounded-lg bg-white d-surface flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="font-bold text-(--color-accent) text-lg shrink-0 w-6">4</span>
        <div>
          <a href="/convening/" class="font-semibold hover:text-(--color-accent) transition-colors">Convening a Group</a>
          <p class="d-text-dim">The social cost of peer learning.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 border-t border-stone-200 d-border">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Use Unpeeragogy with AI</h2>
    <p class="d-text-sec max-w-2xl mb-4">
      Our MCP server exposes failure vectors, prompts, and tools for analyzing patterns
      with AI agents (Claude Desktop, Gemini, etc.).
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 text-sm">
      <a href="/mcp/" class="rounded-lg bg-(--color-accent) px-5 py-2.5 text-white font-semibold hover:bg-(--color-accent-light) transition-colors w-fit">
        MCP Documentation →
      </a>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs d-text-dim px-3">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 d-surface px-2 py-1">API /llms.txt</span>
        <span class="rounded-full bg-stone-100 d-surface px-2 py-1">Prompt template</span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>